==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|LL.}} {{term|proximatus}}, past participle of {{term|proximare||to draw near, approach}}, from {{etyl|la}} {{term|proximus||nearest|lang=la}}, superlative of {{term|prope||near}}.

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# [[close|Close]] or [[closest]]; [[adjacent]].
# {{legal}} Immediately preceding or following in a chain of causation.
# About to take place; [[impending]].

====Antonyms====
* {{sense|w.r.t. causes}} [[ultimate]]

====Related terms====
* [[proximate cause]]

